#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192539 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fd17c91-187c-5849-9648-7b31f2b3be96" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "ea06319a-98d8-5b73-a224-a8c03005b5db" :question/math-academy-id "e-12876" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $10x - 4 > 16$." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $4$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}10x - 4 & > 16 \\\\ 10x - 4 + 4 & > 16 + 4 \\\\ 10x + 0 & > 20 \\\\ 10x & > 20\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $10{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}10x & > 20 \\\\ \\frac{10x}{10} & > \\frac{20}{10} \\\\ \\frac{10x}{10} & > 2 \\\\ x & > 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x> 2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192540 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cb884d3-1a4f-56aa-8628-b899f4eefacb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities When Flipping is Required"}] :question/id #uuid "1107a2bf-525e-5a08-9f28-dfd8c72718c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-12877" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-2x + 3 > -1$." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $3$ from both sides:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2x + 3 & > - 1 \\\\ -2x + 3 - 3 & > - 1 - 3 \\\\ -2x + 0 & > - 4 \\\\ -2x & > - 4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-2$.\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2x & > - 4 \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2} & <\\frac{-4}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2} & <2 \\\\ x & <2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x<2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192541 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6076650-101c-5fbf-bf47-9de8e6888288" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality and Adjusting the Final Result"}] :question/id #uuid "fa636b0d-3494-56b7-8be2-b634316f60ab" :question/math-academy-id "e-12878" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-11 \\le -8y + 5$." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $5$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & \\le - 8y + 5 \\\\ -11 - 5 & \\le - 8y + 5 - 5 \\\\ -16 & \\le - 8y + 0 \\\\ -16 & \\le - 8y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-8$.\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-16 & \\le- 8y \\\\ \\frac{-16}{-8} & \\ge\\frac{-8y}{-8} \\\\ 2 & \\ge\\frac{-8y}{-8} \\\\ 2 & \\gey\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\ny \\le 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\ny \\le 2\n$$"}]}
